    "convention": "Each indicator is first reverse scored where flagged ((min + max) - x), then rescaled to 0-100 as (x - min)/(max - min)*100 with its declared original scale endpoints (never the observed minimum/maximum). Classic PLS-SEM (no consistency correction; same inner weighting scheme, iteration cap and tolerance as the main fit) is re-estimated on the rescaled data. Unstandardized outer weights = standardized weight / sd(rescaled indicator), normalized to sum to 1 within each block; construct score = weighted sum of the rescaled indicators (0-100 when no weight is negative). Performance = mean construct score (constructs) or mean rescaled indicator (indicators), on the 0-100 scale. Importance = unstandardized total effect of the construct on the target: OLS of each endogenous score on its predictors' scores gives B, total effects = (I - B)^-1 - I. Indicator importance = normalized weight x the construct's importance. Negative importance keeps its sign. Constructs listed are all predecessors of the target (any directed path); 'direct' means a direct structural path exists. Point estimates only (no bootstrap intervals)."
